# Commit Message Workflow (mandatory)

Before creating any `git commit` in this repository:

- Use the project skill `/commit-message-wrapper`.
- Read and apply `.cursor/skills/commit-message-wrapper/SKILL.md`.
- Draft the message using the skill's required template before running
  `git commit`.
- Pass the commit message using the skill's HEREDOC wrapper.
- Do not use an inline one-line commit message for repository commits.
- If the wrapper or template cannot be followed, stop and ask the user before
  committing.
